          "id": 797773161,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, because Portugal was on CET in 1970. Switched to CET in the mid '60s, switched back in 1976. I think perhaps it was legally referred to as year round summer time, but Unix codes it as just being on CET.",
